  "_title": "Four bits at once — the 74HC283",
  "_description": "Eight switches in, five LEDs out: a whole 4-bit adder in one 16-pin package. Inside it is four of the full adder you just built, chained carry to carry. Read A on the left bank, B on the right, and the answer across the LEDs (the red one is the carry, worth 16). Note the engine spells the bit slices a0..a3 — a0 is the ONES bit.",
